      "message": "just spitballin\u0027 here:\n\n  name \u003d None\n  domain_id \u003d None\n\n  if \u0027name\u0027 in args[2]\n    name \u003d args[2][\u0027name\u0027]\n  if \u0027domain_id\u0027 in args[2]\n    domain_id \u003d args[2][\u0027domain_id\u0027]\n\n  msg \u003d \u0027Duplicate entry\u0027\n  if name:\n    msg \u003d msg + \u0027 found with name %s\u0027 % name\n  if domain_id\n     msg \u003d msg + \u0027 at domain ID %s\u0027 % domain_id\n\n  raise exception.Conflict(type\u003dconflict_type, details\u003dmsg)\n\nThis way, you fall back to the existing message if args[2] has nothing helpful. If if has name and domain ID (which you\u0027ll need for groups, users and projects) you have a more helpful message. And it\u0027ll work for domains, endpoints, regions and roles (maybe?), too.",
